Walsh SW. Matrix Metalloproteinase 1 Causes Vasoconstriction and Enhances Vessel Reactivity to Angiotensin II via Protease-Activated Receptor 1. Reproductive sciences 2016;23:542–8. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [105]. Levine RJ, Maynard SE, Qian C, Lim KH, England LJ, Yu KF, et al. Circulating angiogenic factors and the risk of preeclampsia. N Engl J Med 2004;350:672–83. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [106]. LaMarca BB, Bennett WA, Alexander BT, Cockrell K, Granger JP. Hypertension produced by reductions in uterine perfusion in the pregnant rat: role of tumor necrosis factor-alpha. Hypertension 2005;46:1022–5. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [107]. LaMarca BD, Ryan MJ, Gilbert JS, Murphy SR, Granger JP. Inflammatory cytokines in the pathophysiology of hypertension during preeclampsia. Curr Hypertens Rep 2007;9:480–5. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [108]. Xia Y, Ramin SM, Kellems RE. Potential roles of angiotensin receptor-activating autoantibody in the pathophysiology of preeclampsia. Hypertension 2007;50:269–75. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [109]. LaMarca B, Wallukat G, Llinas M, Herse F, Dechend R, Granger JP. Autoantibodies to the angiotensin type I receptor in response to placental ischemia and tumor necrosis factor alpha in pregnant rats. Hypertension 2008;52:1168–72. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [110]. Shah DA, Khalil RA. Bioactive factors in uteroplacental and systemic circulation link placental ischemia to generalized vascular dysfunction in hypertensive pregnancy and preeclampsia. Biochemical pharmacology 2015;95:211–26. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [111]. Levine RJ, Lam C, Qian C, Yu KF, Maynard SE, Sachs BP, et al. Soluble endoglin and other circulating antiangiogenic factors in preeclampsia. The New England journal of medicine 2006;355:992–1005. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [112]. Colson A, Depoix CL, Lamber