pgraded their clinical lifesaving and teaching skills UNFPA 2018 [ 64 ] MHTF Annual 2017 and Review of Phase II (2014–2017) Report Report highlighted annual and MHTF Phase II achievements, challenges, lessons learnt and way forward 33 countries across five regions (the Arab States, West and Central Africa, East and Southern Africa, Asia and the Pacific, and Latin America and the Caribbean). Clinical and teaching skills; EmONC Implemented through numerous global and national partners who strategically designed and delivered the programmes in the countries Strengthened capacity of 765 midwifery tutors in clinical and teaching skills and EmONC UNFPA 2017 [ 65 ] MHTF Phase II Progress (2014–2017) Report Report highlighted progress of implementation of Phase II period including enablers and drivers of change and key results 39 high-morbidity and mortality countries across five regions (the Arab States, West and Central Africa, East and Southern Africa, Asia and the Pacific, and Latin America and the Caribbean). Clinical and teaching skills in EmONC Implemented through numerous global and national partners who strategically designed and delivered the programmes in the countries Trained and strengthened capacity of 710 tutors in clinical and teaching skills and EmONC UNFPA 2014 [ 66 ] MHTF Annual Report 2014 Report highlighted 2008–2013 achievements, challenges, lessons learnt and way forward post-MDGs 42 high priority countries across five regions (the Arab States, West and Central Africa, East and Southern Africa, Asia and the Pacific, and Latin America and the Caribbean). EmONC, HMS and HBB; Competency Based Education (CBE) Training – effective competency-based teaching, learning and assessment strategies; basic supervision Implemented through numerous global and national partners who strategically designed and delivered the programmes in the countries Over 1,200 midwifery tutors upgraded their skills to provide competency-based education and training as well as materna